<mxCell id="t13c45" value="&lt;b&gt;Both directions at once&lt;/b&gt; is common: validate a BST (range down, verdict up). If a parent needs two facts per child, return a tuple instead of calling height() again from every node, which makes skewed trees O(N²)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="444" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
